    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "When should we involve RJY Group for Leadership Team?",
        "answer": "Involve RJY Group when conditions, recurring faults, planned upgrades, audit findings, staffing constraints, or operational risk require a structured technical review. Early coordination helps clarify dependencies, available records, work windows, responsible stakeholders, and the safest practical next step."
      },
      {
        "question": "What information helps start a Leadership Team conversation?",
        "answer": "Share the facility location, affected assets, operating symptoms, known history, current maintenance records, urgency, access constraints, and desired outcome. Photographs, trend data, alarm history, drawings, test reports, and stakeholder contacts can help make the first review more productive."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can Leadership Team work be planned around active operations?",
        "answer": "Yes. Planning can account for occupied spaces, critical schedules, restricted access, safety controls, infection-control requirements, academic calendars, production windows, and approved outages. The exact approach depends on site conditions, system redundancy, and the consequence of interruption."
      },
      {
        "question": "How does RJY Group define priorities for Leadership Team?",
        "answer": "Priorities are developed by considering observed condition, operational consequence, safety, compliance needs, redundancy, service history, maintainability, access, available resources, and timing. This creates a practical sequence instead of treating every finding as equally urgent or equally valuable."
      },
      {
        "question": "Will we receive documentation after the Leadership Team review?",
        "answer": "The appropriate records depend on the agreed scope, but work can include condition notes, completed-service documentation, test results, photographs, open issues, corrective recommendations, and next-step priorities. Deliverables should be confirmed before field work begins so expectations remain clear."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can Leadership Team be coordinated with other facility services?",
        "answer": "Yes. RJY Group can connect building automation, HVAC, standby power, water treatment, technical staffing, and operational technology security where systems interact. Coordinated planning helps teams see dependencies, avoid conflicting changes, and organize work around the facility mission."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do we request a scope for Leadership Team?",
        "answer": "Use the enquiry form with the facility, system, concern, timing, and preferred contact, or call the Houston office. An initial conversation can determine whether the next step should be records review, site inspection, technical assessment, service visit, or proposal development."
      }
    ],
    "phoneCta": "Discuss leadership team with an RJY Group facilities specialist.",
